<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>Authorize #{@request.client.client_name || "an MCP client"} — GoCD</title>
    <style>
      body {
        background: #f4f8f9;
        min-height: 100vh;
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        justify-content: center;
        font-family: "Open Sans", "Helvetica Neue", helvetica, arial, sans-serif;
        margin: 0;
        color: #333;
      }
      .card {
        background: white;
        border: 1px solid #d6e0e2;
        border-radius: 6px;
        box-shadow: 0 2px 12px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.08);
        width: 100%;
        max-width: 520px;
        padding: 28px 32px;
        box-sizing: border-box;
      }
      h1 {
        font-size: 20px;
        margin: 0 0 12px;
      }
      p {
        line-height: 1.5;
        margin: 0 0 12px;
        font-size: 14px;
      }
      .who {
        background: #eef4f5;
        border-radius: 4px;
        padding: 10px 12px;
        font-size: 13px;
        margin-bottom: 16px;
      }
      .actions {
        display: flex;
        gap: 10px;
        justify-content: flex-end;
        margin-top: 20px;
      }
      button {
        font: inherit;
        font-size: 14px;
        padding: 8px 18px;
        border-radius: 4px;
        border: 1px solid transparent;
        cursor: pointer;
      }
      .allow {
        background: #1f7a1f;
        color: white;
      }
      .deny {
        background: white;
        color: #444;
        border-color: #b9c7ca;
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main class="card">
      <h1>Authorize {assigns.request.client.client_name || "an MCP client"}</h1>

      <p class="who">
        Signed in as <strong>{@user.display_name || @user.username}</strong>. {if @user.roles !=
                                                                                    nil and
                                                                                    "admin" in (@user.roles ||
                                                                                                  []),
                                                                                  do:
                                                                                    "This account administers the server.",
                                                                                  else:
                                                                                    "This account acts with its own permissions."}
      </p>

      <p>
        This client asks to act on <strong>this GoCD server</strong> as you: to read
        pipelines, stages, jobs, agents and analytics, and — only where your account
        may — to trigger, pause, approve and cancel work.
      </p>

      <p>
        Approving issues an access token. It appears in your access tokens list as <em>“MCP client: {assigns.request.client.client_name || assigns.request.client.client_id}”</em>,
        and revoking it there ends this client's access.
      </p>

      <form method="POST" action="/oauth/authorize">
        <input type="hidden" name="_csrf_token" value={@csrf_token} />
        <input type="hidden" name="response_type" value="code" />
        <input type="hidden" name="client_id" value={@request.client.client_id} />
        <input type="hidden" name="redirect_uri" value={@request.redirect_uri} />
        <input type="hidden" name="code_challenge" value={@request.code_challenge} />
        <input type="hidden" name="code_challenge_method" value="S256" />
        <input type="hidden" name="scope" value={@request.scope || ""} />
        <input type="hidden" name="state" value={@request.state || ""} />

        <div class="actions">
          <button class="deny" type="submit" name="decision" value="deny">Deny</button>
          <button class="allow" type="submit" name="decision" value="approve">Allow</button>
        </div>
      </form>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
